## 15. Spring Boot Auth service

Package root: `com.example.backendspringboot`.

### Config

`application.yaml`:

- Imports optional `../.env`.
- Datasource MySQL URL with timezone Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh.
- JPA `ddl-auto: none`, physical naming standard.
- Redis host default currently literal `localhost` unless overridden by env in docker-compose.
- Mail host/port/user/password from SMTP env.
- Google OAuth client id/secret/redirect.
- `server.port=8080`.
- JWT:
  - `jwt.signerKey`
  - `jwt.refreshSignerKey`
  - `jwt.accessTokenExpiration` seconds default 28800
  - `jwt.refreshTokenExpiration` seconds default 604800
- App:
  - `frontend-url`
  - `cookie.secure`
  - `smtp.from`
  - `otp.expires-in-seconds`
  - `password-reset.expires-in-seconds`

### Security

`SecurityConfig`:

- BCryptPasswordEncoder bean.
- CSRF disabled.
- CORS enabled:
  - allowed origins hardcoded `http://localhost:5173`
  - methods GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS
  - headers `*`
  - credentials true
- All requests permitAll. Auth is enforced inside services by reading cookies/tokens, not by Spring filter chain.

### Entities and repositories

- `Account` maps `TAI_KHOAN`; fields accountId, username, password, email, accountType, isPasswordChanged, isActive. Implements `AccountInfo`.
- `RefreshToken` maps `REFRESH_TOKENS`; id integer identity, accountId, token, expiresAt.
- `LoginAttempt` maps `DANG_NHAP_THAT_BAI`; composite key username + LocalDate date, attemptCount.
- `AccountRepository`: findByUsername, findByEmail.
- `RefreshTokenRepository`: findByTokenAndExpiresAtAfter, deleteByToken.
- `LoginAttemptRepository`: findByUsernameAndDate, deleteByUsernameAndDate.
- `AccountType` enum contains db role values and profile SQL for admin/ctsv/khoa/covan/sinhvien.
- `AccountMapper.toUserMap(Account)`: load role profile by account type using JdbcTemplate; returns same field shape as Node auth user.

### Auth controller

Base path `/api/auth`.

- `POST /login`: body `ten_tai_khoan`, `mat_khau`; sets accessToken/refreshToken httpOnly cookies; returns user map directly.
- `POST /logout`: deletes refresh token, clears cookies; returns `{message}`.
- `POST /refresh-token`: reads refresh cookie, rotates tokens, returns user.
- `GET /me`: reads access cookie, returns user.
- `POST /change-password`: body `mat_khau_cu`, `mat_khau_moi`, `nhap_lai_mat_khau_moi`; returns `{message}`.
- `POST /forgot-password`: body `email`; returns OTP token data.
- `POST /verify-reset-otp`: body `otp_token`, `otp`; returns reset token.
- `POST /reset-password`: body `reset_token`, `mat_khau_moi`, `nhap_lai_mat_khau_moi`.
- `GET /google/login`: returns `{url}`.
- `GET /google/callback?code=...`: exchanges code, sets cookies, redirects to `${FRONTEND_URL}/login?google=success`.

Cookie utility:

- Adds cookies with HttpOnly, SameSite Strict, path `/`, maxAge duration, Secure from `app.cookie.secure`.
- Access cookie duration 8 hours.
- Refresh cookie duration 7 days.

### AuthenticationService

- Login:
  - max 5 failed attempts per username per date.
  - find account by username.
  - BCrypt password match.
  - check active.
  - clear attempts and build session.
- Build session:
  - user map via mapper.
  - access token via `JwtService.generateAccessToken(user, accessTokenExpiration)`.
  - refresh token via `generateRefreshToken(accountId, refreshTokenExpiration)`.
  - save refresh token expires `now + refreshTokenExpiration`.
- Refresh:
  - token must exist in DB and not expired.
  - verify refresh JWT.
  - load active account.
  - delete old token and build new session.
- Me:
  - verify access JWT.
  - load active account.
  - return user map.
- Change password:
  - validate new/confirm match and size via validation annotations.
  - call `me(accessToken)` to get account id.
  - validate old password.
  - encode and set `isPasswordChanged=true`.

### JwtService

- Implements HS256 manually with Base64 URL no padding, HmacSHA256, constant-time signature compare.
- Access token claims: full user map + `iat`, `exp`, `jti`, `sub = ma_tai_khoan`.
- Refresh token claims: `ma_tai_khoan`, `type='refresh'`, `iat`, `exp`.
- `verifyAccessToken` and `verifyRefreshToken`; refresh requires type refresh.
- `parseToken` returns `JwtInfo` for CustomJwtDecoder.

### OtpService

- Mirrors Node OTP logic.
- `forgotPassword`:
  - requires `spring.mail.username`.
  - find active account by email.
  - generate 6-digit OTP with SecureRandom.
  - OTP token secret = signerKey + ":" + current bcrypt password + ":otp".
  - OTP hash sha256(accountId + ":" + otp + ":" + signerKey).
  - send HTML email through `SendMailService`.
  - return `otp_token`, `expires_in` as seconds string like `300s`.
- `verifyResetOtp`:
  - decode JWT payload without verify.
  - verify signature+expiry with otp secret.
  - compare otp hash.
  - issue reset token signed with reset secret signerKey + ":" + current password.
- `resetPassword`:
  - check new/confirm match.
  - decode and verify reset token.
  - set password encoded and `isPasswordChanged=true`.

### Google OAuth

- `buildGoogleLoginUrl`: Google auth endpoint with client_id, redirect_uri, response_type code, scope `openid email profile`, access_type offline, prompt select_account.
- Callback:
  - POST code to `https://oauth2.googleapis.com/token`.
  - GET userinfo from `https://www.googleapis.com/oauth2/v3/userinfo`.
  - require verified email.
  - find existing account by email, active.
  - issue same app JWT/cookies.
  - Does not create accounts.

### Exceptions

Response shape from Spring errors is `ApiResponse`:

```json
{ "code": 4005, "message": "Sai ten tai khoan hoac mat khau", "result": null }
```

Important `ErrorCode` values:

- 1001 UNAUTHENTICATED -> 401
- 1002 INVALID_TOKEN -> 401
- 4003 ACCOUNT_NOT_EXISTED -> 400
- 4004 ACCOUNT_BLOCKED -> 401
- 4005 INVALID_CREDENTIALS -> 401
- 4006 ROLE_PROFILE_NOT_FOUND -> 403
- 4007 TOO_MANY_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS -> 429
- 4008 BAD_REQUEST -> 400
- 4009 EMAIL_NOT_FOUND -> 400
- 4010 SMTP_NOT_CONFIGURED -> 400
- 4011 INVALID_OTP -> 400
- 4012 OTP_EXPIRED -> 400
- 4013 OTP_WRONG -> 400
- 4014 INVALID_RESET_TOKEN -> 400
- 4015 RESET_TOKEN_EXPIRED -> 400
- 4016 PASSWORD_MISMATCH -> 400
- 4017 PASSWORD_TOO_SHORT -> 400
- 4018 OLD_PASSWORD_WRONG -> 400
- 4019 MAIL_SEND_FAILED -> 500

## 16. Frontend architecture

### Entry and routing

`main.jsx` renders:

- `BrowserRouter`
- `AuthProvider`
- `App`
- CSS `src/styles/main.css`

`App.jsx` routes:

- `/login` -> `LoginPage`
- `/forgot-password` -> `ForgotPasswordPage`
- `/change-password` -> `ChangePasswordPage`
- `/` -> `Home` role router:
  - no user -> `/login`
  - user but `da_doi_mk=false` -> `/change-password`
  - admin -> `AdminDashboard`
  - ctsv -> `CtsvDashboard`
  - khoa -> `KhoaDashboard`
  - covan -> `CovanDashboard`
  - sinhvien -> `SinhVienDashboard`
- `/notifications` -> `ProtectedRoute` -> `NotificationsPage`

### Axios client

`api = axios.create({ baseURL: VITE_API_URL || http://localhost:5000/api, withCredentials:true })`.

Request interceptor:

- If `config.url` starts with `/auth` or `auth`, set `baseURL = VITE_SPRING_BOOT_API_URL || http://localhost:8080/api`.

Response interceptor:

- On 401, if not `/auth/refresh-token` or `/auth/login`, queue concurrent failed requests while refreshing.
- Calls `POST /auth/refresh-token`.
- Replays original request on success.
- On refresh failure dispatches `window` event `auth:unauthorized`.

### AuthContext

- State initialized from `localStorage.user`.
- `loading=true` until `refreshMe` attempt completes.
- `login(credentials)`: POST `/auth/login`, store user in localStorage.
- `loginWithGoogle()`: GET `/auth/google/login`, redirect to URL in `data.url` or `data.result`.
- `refreshMe()`: GET `/auth/me`, store user.
- `changePassword(payload)`: POST `/auth/change-password`, then refreshMe.
- `logout()`: POST `/auth/logout` best effort, clear local user.
- On mount refreshMe; on `auth:unauthorized`, clear user.

### ProtectedRoute

- While loading: show page status.
- No user -> `/login`.
- Password not changed -> `/change-password`.
- If `roles` prop provided and role not included -> `/`.

### AppLayout

Common shell with fixed left sidebar 260px, content area, brand link, role-specific nav, bottom user menu.

Role labels:

- admin: Quan tri vien
- ctsv: Phong CTSV
- khoa: Truong Khoa
- covan: Co van hoc tap
- sinhvien: Sinh vien

Default nav:

- khoa: Notifications, Assignment (`/?view=assignment`), Employees (`/?view=employees`), History (`/?view=history`)
- ctsv: Notifications, Create (`/?view=create`), Students (`/?view=students`), Assignments (`/?view=assignments`), History (`/?view=history`)
- covan: Overview `/`, Notifications
- sinhvien: Overview `/`, Notifications

Unread indicators:

- Uses localStorage keys:
  - `read_notification_ids:${ma_tai_khoan}`
  - `seen_khoa_assignments`
  - `seen_khoa_replacements`
  - `seen_ctsv_assignments`
  - `seen_ctsv_replacements`
  - `seen_khoa_assignment_details`
- Polls every 15 seconds.
- Khoa unread assignment if assignments waiting `Chờ phân công` or replacement requests in `Chờ duyệt`/`Khoa đang duyệt` not seen.
- CTSV unread assignment if assignment status `Chờ giám đốc duyệt` or replacement in `Khoa đã duyệt`/`Giám đốc đang duyệt`.

### DataTable

Props: `columns`, `rows`, `actions`, `actionLabel`, `filterable`, `pageSize`.

- Column fields: `key`, `label`, optional `render(row)`, `renderText(row)`, `width`, `minWidth`, `align`, `type`.
- Built-in default widths and number-center alignment.
- Filtering per column if `filterable`.
