## 22. Known caveats to preserve or intentionally fix

- Spring Security currently permits all requests; auth logic is service-level. If changing this, update frontend and exception handling carefully.
- Spring `CustomJwtAuthenticationConverter.getStatus()` compares status to `"BLOCKED"` but `Account.getStatus()` returns `"true"`/`"false"`; this converter is effectively unused because all requests are permitAll.
- Spring CORS origin is hardcoded to `http://localhost:5173`, while Node uses `FRONTEND_URL`.
- Node auth route cookie access maxAge is hardcoded 15 minutes even env `JWT_EXPIRES_IN` may be `8h`.
- Frontend AppLayout injects substantial inline CSS overriding `main.css`; reproduce it or move equivalent CSS to stylesheet.
- The repo contains real-looking SMTP values in local `.env`; do not propagate them.
